-- title:
--   Proposition 4.4 — common image π_m(Λ_p⁺) = G_m
-- statement:
--   For every prime $p\equiv1\pmod4$ and every $m\ge3$,
--   $$\pi_m(\Lambda_p^+)=G_m,$$
--   where $\Lambda_p$ is the group generated by the classes of $A(p)$ in the projective unit group of $L(\mathbb Z[1/p])$ and $\Lambda_p^+$ is its subgroup of words of even length.
--
--   The vertex group $G_m$ of order $2^{3m-4}$ is therefore the same for every prime $p\equiv1\pmod8$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: π_m(Λ_p⁺), the image of the even-length words in the classes of A(p) → the subgroup of Ĝ_m generated by the elements π_m(a)π_m(b), a, b ∈ A(p); reason: Λ_p⁺ is generated by the products of two generators (the generating set is inverse-closed, [ā] = [a]⁻¹), and π_m is a homomorphism on Λ_p, so the image of Λ_p⁺ is generated by these images; same group
--   - encoding: A(n) = {a ∈ L(ℤ) : N(a) = n, a₀ odd}/{±1} → the set APos n of representatives with positive real part; a product of classes is written sgnNorm of the product of representatives; reason: the real part of each element is odd, hence nonzero, so each class has exactly one representative with a₀ > 0; same instances
--   - encoding: π_m : 1 + 2L(ℤ₂) → Ĝ_m (reduction mod 2^m, then the quotient by scalars), Ĝ_m = U_m/R_m^×, G_m the norm ≡ 1 (mod 8) classes → pim m on integral quaternions (value 1 off the domain a ≡ 1 mod 2); U_m the units of L(ℤ/2^m) reducing to 1 mod 2; G_m the image of the units with norm ≡ 1 (mod 2^min(m,3)); reason: every quaternion the source reduces in this statement is integral and ≡ 1 (mod 2); for m ≥ 3 the groups are those of Definition 4.1
-- source:
--   Yali Aharon Holzman, Michael Ilan, Assaf Reiner, Amnon Ta-Shma, Full-Rank Constructions of Explicit Lossless Expanders and Good Small-Set qLTCs, STOC 2027 submission #692 (October 2026), Proposition 4.4, p. 21 (printed page = PDF page)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FullRankSmallSetQLTC_IndependentChecks_Quaternion

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace FullRankSmallSetQLTC.IndependentChecks

open Quaternion Pointwise

/-- **Proposition 4.4** (Common image, p. 21). For every prime `p ≡ 1 (mod 4)` and every `m ≥ 3`,
`π_m(Λ_p⁺) = G_m`. Here `Λ_p⁺`, the words of even length in the classes of `A(p)`, is the
subgroup generated by the products `[a][b]`, `a, b ∈ A(p)` (the generating set is closed under
inverses, `[ā] = [a]⁻¹`), so its image under the homomorphism `π_m` is the subgroup of `Ĝ_m`
generated by the `π_m(a)π_m(b)`. -/
theorem proposition_4_4 (p : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) (hp4 : p % 4 = 1) (m : ℕ) (hm : 3 ≤ m) :
    Subgroup.closure {g : GHat m | ∃ a ∈ APos p, ∃ b ∈ APos p, g = pim m a * pim m b} =
      Gm m := by sorry

end FullRankSmallSetQLTC.IndependentChecks
